<p>Google Ads is the fastest way to get your business in front of people actively searching for what you sell. Unlike social media where you interrupt people, Google Ads reach people at the exact moment they are looking for your product or service. This guide walks you through everything you need to run a profitable campaign in Kenya from day one.</p>

<h2>Understanding How Google Ads Works</h2>

<p>Google Ads operates on an auction system. Every time someone searches on Google, an auction takes place in milliseconds. Advertisers bid on keywords — the words people type into Google. The winner of the auction gets their ad shown, but they only pay when someone actually clicks (this is called Pay-Per-Click or PPC).</p>

<p>Your position in the auction is determined not just by your bid but by your <strong>Quality Score</strong> — a measure of how relevant your ad and landing page are to the search query. A high Quality Score means you can outrank competitors while paying less per click.</p>

<h2>Step 1: Set Up Your Google Ads Account</h2>

<ol>
  <li>Go to ads.google.com and sign in with your Google account</li>
  <li>Click "New Campaign"</li>
  <li>For your first campaign, select the goal "Website traffic" or "Leads"</li>
  <li>Choose "Search" as your campaign type — this is text ads that appear in Google search results</li>
  <li>Set your location to Kenya (or specific cities: Nairobi, Mombasa, Kisumu etc.)</li>
  <li>Set your language to English (and Swahili if relevant)</li>
</ol>

