<h2>Step 2: Keyword Research</h2>

<p>Keywords are the searches that will trigger your ads. Getting this right is the most important step in the entire process. Use Google Keyword Planner (free inside Google Ads) to find:</p>

<ul>
  <li>Search volume: how many people search for this term per month in Kenya</li>
  <li>Competition: how many advertisers are bidding on it</li>
  <li>Suggested bid: what you might expect to pay per click</li>
</ul>

<h3>Keyword Match Types Explained</h3>

<p>This is where most beginners make expensive mistakes:</p>

<ul>
  <li><strong>Broad Match</strong> (default): Your ad can show for any variation, even loosely related searches. Dangerous for beginners — wastes budget. Example: bidding on "shoes" could show your ad for "how to clean shoes".</li>
  <li><strong>Phrase Match</strong> "keyword": Your ad shows when the search contains your phrase in order. Much safer. Example: "digital marketing agency" would show for "best digital marketing agency Nairobi".</li>
  <li><strong>Exact Match</strong> [keyword]: Your ad only shows for that exact search. Highest relevance, lowest waste. Example: [plumber Nairobi] only shows when someone types exactly "plumber Nairobi".</li>
</ul>

<blockquote>Start with Phrase and Exact match only. Never use Broad Match until you understand negative keywords. It will burn your budget in days.</blockquote>

<h2>Step 3: Write Compelling Ads</h2>

<p>A Google Search ad has these components:</p>

<ul>
  <li><strong>Headlines</strong>: Up to 15 headlines of 30 characters each. Google rotates them. Include your keyword in at least one.</li>
  <li><strong>Descriptions</strong>: Up to 4 descriptions of 90 characters each. Use these to explain your offer and include a CTA.</li>
  <li><strong>Final URL</strong>: The page people land on after clicking. Must be directly relevant to the ad.</li>
</ul>

<h3>High-Performing Ad Formula</h3>
<ul>
  <li>Headline 1: Include the keyword. "Digital Marketing Agency Nairobi"</li>
  <li>Headline 2: Your key benefit. "Grow Your Business Online Fast"</li>
  <li>Headline 3: A differentiator or offer. "Free Strategy Session — Book Today"</li>
  <li>Description 1: Expand on the benefit and add social proof. "We've helped 39+ Kenyan brands increase leads by 300%. SEO, Ads, Social Media under one roof."</li>
  <li>Description 2: CTA with urgency. "Limited slots available. Book your free 30-minute strategy call today."</li>
</ul>

